hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-7 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-7 = cons "*Correct* is *cor-regere*, to make fully straight, from the root that gives *rex*, *rule*, *regular*, *right* and *direct*. An *address* is the same root again: *ad* + *directiare*, to direct toward. So in the 1970 decision to identify a thing by its location, the address was a direction: go here and you'll find it. Content addressing turns that inside out. The direction is computed from what the thing is. You don't go somewhere to find it; it is its own direction. Right, rule, direct and address were always one family; in hyperactivity they finally point at the same object." (cons "" nil)
